1
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:10,399
I do struggle with enduring the non-doing of\h
certain things out of faith or trust in the instruction,

2
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:16,799
since doing so is actually a pretty\h
painful process. My impression is that the way I\h\h

3
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:22,399
dealt with unwholesome things in the past\h
stands in the way here. Whenever I felt the\h\h

4
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:29,439
habit was not good, like drinking, smoking, or\h
eating a bag of crisps, I continued doing it,\h\h

5
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:35,439
but was consciously paying attention to the\h
drawbacks - how I felt afterwards, and so on -

6
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:42,559
until I could let go naturally. This seems like\h
a much more gradual and less painful approach.\h\h

7
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:49,199
I do not need to restrain myself that much, have\h
my own experience of a criteria for good and bad\h\h

8
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:56,399
and I factually do let go of bad habits that way.\h
What is the benefit or advantage to say "no" to\h\h

9
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:05,360
things in the way that you teach and enduring\h
much more pain than I seem to need to endure?

10
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:13,519
Well, the first thing to understand here is that\h
the pain that comes with enduring things is not in\h\h

11
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:24,639
fact caused by the restraint. It's caused by the\h
unabandoned craving and attachment. So through\h\h

12
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:32,319
restraining yourself rightly - which begins by\h
keeping five precepts and then adding the celibacy\h\h

13
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:38,959
and also the nondistraction - what will happen\h
is that your mind becomes more outlined.

14
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:47,439
And so there's going to be this inner struggle between\h
you saying "no" to things and the mind still wanting it.

15
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:54,079
And that internal conflict, that battle\h
between you on the one hand and citta on the\h\h

16
00:01:54,080 --> 00:02:01,599
other hand, that is what is being revealed through\h
the restraint. But it is not the restraint that is\h\h

17
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:10,160
causing the pain. It is the mind, citta, still being\h
wild and untamed that is causing the pain here.\h\h

18
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:18,719
So then to say I am only going to gradually give\h
things up; that's actually a wrong understanding\h\h

19
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:24,559
of what the gradual training is. The gradual\h
training begins by keeping the eight precepts,\h\h

20
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:29,999
or as I just said, five precepts and then plus\h
celibacy and non-distraction. That is where\h\h

21
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,599
the gradual training begins. But if you say I'm\h
going to only give things up gradually, then you\h\h

22
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:43,599
are still giving very mixed messages to the mind.\h
Sometimes you give in because you say otherwise it\h\h

23
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:49,519
becomes too painful, and sometimes you say "no" and\h
in that situation there is not really any taming\h\h

24
00:02:49,520 --> 00:03:01,359
or training of the mind. So by analogy, a parent\h
is responsible for its child. And if the child\h\h

25
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:06,159
is going to throw a tantrum because it wants\h
something and you're not giving it, then the\h\h

26
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:14,399
easy thing to do is to still give the child what\h
it wants because it would immediately shut up.\h\h

27
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:19,359
But at the same time, you are giving the child\h
the message that becoming all emotional and\h\h

28
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:25,999
wound up about not getting what it wants is\h
the way for the child to get what it wants.\h\h

29
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:33,679
So if you just look at the immediate, let's say,\hquieting down of the child - which is the mind\h\h

30
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:38,559
in this case - then you are still creating\h
more trouble for yourself in the long run,\h\h

31
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:43,919
because next time when the child wants something\h
it's going to be more emotional because it gets\h\h

32
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:51,999
the message that this is the way to get what\h
it wants. So how to train or educate a child\h\h

33
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:59,519
rightly so that it becomes a mature responsible\h
adult, is to basically never give it what it\h\h

34
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:05,439
wants when it is emotionally invested in it to\h
the point that it makes a drama about it. But\h\h

35
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:11,199
that means that you as the parent have to stand\h
your ground and not be afraid of saying "no".

36
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:17,679
And so you need to endure the upset of the child and\h
that is not a punishment of the child. That is\h\h

37
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:23,039
your responsibility as the parent: for the child\h
to cease being a child and become a responsible\h\h

38
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:28,399
adult that is not going to be "childish" when it\h
doesn't get what it wants. Now it's the same with\h\h

39
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:34,639
the mind. But if the parent sometimes gives in and\h
sometimes doesn't give in then the child is only\h\h

40
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:42,639
going to become more confused. So what needs to\h
be understood here is that the starting point is,\h\h

41
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:48,959
that basically you don't even see that you are\h
a parent. Most people don't even see that they\h\h

42
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:54,319
have a child and that they are responsible for it.\h
So first that needs to be clear. Then you need to\h\h

43
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:59,199
recognize: it's my responsibility to look after\h
that child. And in the beginning that's going\h\h

44
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:04,799
to be unpleasant but that is how it is. I mean, we\h
didn't ask for it but that's the situation you find\h\h

45
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:14,399
yourself in. So you take responsibility and start\h
to gradually train the mind, educate the child.\h\h

46
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:20,479
But gradual means that as the parent you firmly\h
stand your ground and never give in when the\h\h

47
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:29,279
child puts pressure on you. And as a result\h
of that uncompromising virtue - or basically\h\h

48
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:35,359
never ceasing to overlook your responsibility\h
in relation to the child - as a result of that\h\h

49
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:41,359
the child will gradually grow up and become more\h
mature. Right? The mind will become more tamed,\h\h

50
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:47,039
trained, composed. That is the direction where\h
this is going. So gradual training means: yes,\h\h

51
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:53,519
the mind gradually begins to calm down, but you\h
cannot start adopting a gradual attitude from\h\h

52
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:58,159
the beginning by saying I'm sometimes giving in,\h
sometimes not, because otherwise it's too painful.\h\h

53
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:06,959
And if you see that something is not right, why do\h
you still give in? Any giving in to the pressure of\h\h

54
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:14,639
the mind is a weakness on your part. It's basically\h
the parent being bossed around by its own child.\h\h

55
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:23,359
Now, that's a very bad situation to be in. So,\h
it's quite important to be clear that this\h\h

56
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:29,519
is what the training is and you don't know\h
for how long the mind is going to resist you,\h\h

57
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:34,239
how much of a drama it's going to make. Maybe you\h
think it's going to be like this for the rest of\h\h

58
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:42,159
your life, but it might not be. But even if it\h
is, you have to be prepared to then simply endure\h\h

59
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:49,919
whatever impulses and appetites the mind comes up\h
with and not give in, because that is the criteria\h\h

60
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:55,759
for what's wholesome and unwholesome. That's\h
not determined by how the world reacts or what\h\h

61
00:06:55,760 --> 00:07:02,159
your preconceived ideas might be. Unwholesome\h
action means: you giving into the pressure of the\h\h

62
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:08,319
mind,, which is basically the parent forgetting it's\h
a parent and just wanting to be together with the\h\h

63
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:14,319
child and then giving the child higher authority.\h
That's the starting point. That is how this whole\h\h

64
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:19,519
training starts. But it's important to realize\h
it's a very bad situation to be in because there\h\h

65
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:25,919
is no freedom for you and for the mind also not.\h
You are essentially a slave to the impulses and\h\h

66
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:31,599
appetites of your own mind. And the training is\h
to turn that whole situation upside down. And the\h\h

67
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:36,959
mind will resist that because your entire life\h
you have been running with your mind\h\h

68
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:40,959
and you didn't even see that that is what you were\h
doing. So now on account of these instructions you\h\h

69
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:46,719
realize: I have work to do. You are going to set\h
up that boundary. The mind will be running into\h\h

70
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:53,119
it and you have to stand your ground. Basically,\h
there's no other way to tame and train a wild\h\h

71
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:59,999
animal or to educate a child, whichever simile you\h
want to pick. Now, of course, particularly when\h\h

72
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:05,759
it comes to celibacy and nondistraction, that\h
is understandably not going to be easy for many\h\h

73
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:11,919
people, but then the most important thing is to\h
still have the right view. You need\h\h

74
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:18,319
to regard the situation rightly in the sense: it's\h
unacceptable to continue living my life when I'm a\h\h

75
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:24,159
slave of my own mind. I don't want to continue\h
living this way. So even if you occasionally\h\h

76
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:30,079
give in out of carelessness, or you recognize: I'm\h
too weak still, I was just overpowered by my own\h\h

77
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:36,559
mind - that can happen; it's not great but then you\h
quickly reestablish the right perspective. You say:\h\h

78
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:41,199
this is a mistake, this is the wrong direction;
this is contrary to the dhamma - you reestablish\h\h

79
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:49,999
yourself. So that context, that right regarding\h
of your whole existential situation, that needs to\h\h

80
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:57,919
be there, because that is what is going to prevent\h
you tripping up too much. So even if you make\h\h

81
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:02,399
a mistake you correct it and you will only do\h
that if you see it as a mistake. So that's the\h\h

82
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:08,719
first thing and you basically then have to say:\h
it's ridiculous that I cannot live my life and\h\h

83
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:16,719
be comfortable and at ease with myself; that I have\h
to depend on that sexual activity, the distractions\h\h

84
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:21,359
and all the things that go against the precepts.\h
That has to feel like an insult almost, like:\h

85
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:26,399
it's ridiculous that I cannot do this. What is\h
this for nonsense? And so you say: no, from now on\h\h

86
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:33,999
we're going to do something else. And so that\h
is what it means to be accomplished in\h\h

87
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:40,959
self, which curiously the suttas actually talk\h
about. Accomplished in virtue. You are gradually\h\h

88
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:47,759
showing your own mind: look what we've done so far\h
that's not going to continue; from now on I'm\h\h

89
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:52,799
going to say what's right and wrong. And the mind\h
might not immediately listen but at some point it\h\h

90
00:09:52,800 --> 00:10:02,479
will have to. But of course, also: mind will only\h
listen if you, the parent, are not creating any\h\h

91
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:09,119
opportunities for your mind to get back at you,\h
right? If a parent is still drinking, becoming\h\h

92
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:15,039
angry, fighting with people, and so on, then it\h
can say to the child: don't drink, don't smoke, don't\h\h

93
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:20,319
become angry, but the child will say: when I look at you, if you are still doing that,\h\h

94
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:26,639
why should I listen? And that is what the suttas\h
mean by seeing danger in the slightest fault.\h\h

95
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:32,479
That begins by you actually valuing the\h
right things and not making any mistakes, so that\h\h

96
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:39,839
whenever the mind or the child or the animal looks\h
at you, it doesn't see any opening, any opportunity\h\h

97
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:45,519
to get back to you. It cannot accuse you now of\h
being a hypocrite, and then that battle continues.\h\h

98
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:50,959
Every time it looks at you, it sees: oh, this guy\h
is standing his ground. And so at some point\h\h

99
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:56,879
the mind will realize: I cannot play any tricks\h
anymore now. So I have to deal with this guy.\h\h

100
00:10:56,880 --> 00:11:03,279
So let me work together. And that is when the mind\h
becomes pliable. It actually begins to listen to\h\h

101
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:09,119
your instructions. And that is what many people do\h
not actually get. If you're not established in the\h\h

102
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:15,039
virtue first, you can contemplate even the right\h
things, the right themes that the Buddha talks\h\h

103
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:20,159
about,  that we read in the suttas,\h
but as long as that relationship between you and\h\h

104
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:24,319
your mind is not established properly, this is\h
never going to land. Because the practice of the\h\h

105
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:28,959
dhamma is not about you having the right ideas;\h
it's about the mind understanding for itself that\h\h

106
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:34,559
it's painful to crave, to become angry, to hold on\h
to things on account of all sorts of wrong views\h\h

107
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:39,919
and understandings. So in order for the mind to\h
get it, you need to create a situation where the\h\h

108
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:45,679
mind will listen to you. That is what the virtue\h
is about and the sense restraint and then, you know,\h\h

109
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:51,439
not indulging in food and not too much sleep and\h
so on. That is the second\h\h

110
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:56,639
way in which training is gradual. Gradual doesn't\h
mean it's slow. Gradual means that things need\h\h

111
00:11:56,640 --> 00:12:01,919
to happen in a certain order. Virtue, sense\h
restraint, moderation in eating, not sleeping\h\h

112
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:07,999
too much and so on. That's one way in which the.\h
gradual training is gradual - stepwise training.\h\h

113
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:13,679
And the second way in which the gradual training\h
is gradual, is that if you are uncompromising in\h\h

114
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:20,879
your virtue, seeing danger in the slightest fault,\h
only then is there a possibility for the mind to\h\h

115
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:28,559
realize: I can't escape this guy. He's always\h
there. He whenever I look at him, he is there\h\h

116
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:33,519
looking at me. And so you have to start working\h
together. And so the mind begins to listen to you.\h\h

117
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:38,479
That's how the mind becomes composed. And that is\h
when the conflict and the opposition between you\h\h

118
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:45,919
and your own mind gradually wears away. And so\h
the pain that you initially experienced on

119
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:51,919
account of the restraint, which was you over against\h
your mind, that whole situation has now altered,\h\h

120
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:59,439
and your mind becomes your ally rather than your\h
enemy, on account of establishing yourself in\h\h

121
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:04,959
virtue and understanding this principle. 
But\hif your approach from the beginning is\h\h

122
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:08,959
gradual and you still say: well this is going to\h
be too painful, let me every now and again give in,\h\h

123
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:13,679
none of this is going to happen, because you keep\h
giving these mixed messages and the mind will then\h\h

124
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:22,719
never listen to you when it's really important.\h
So that's the principle to understand here.

125
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:29,679
Yes. I thought as well that you basically\h
make yourself dependent on whatever the mind\h\h

126
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:37,039
thinks is unpleasant and pleasant, but you\h
actually don't present it the context where\h\h

127
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:41,919
you say: look even though you might think\h
this is still good, it's actually not good.\h\h

128
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:46,959
So we basically still take the criteria\h
of the mind rather than establishing the

129
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:52,079
criteria from the suttas or from the\h
Buddha himself. Yes. And so\h\h

130
00:13:52,080 --> 00:14:08,960
that is why the mind is in need of
training, of right understanding.